{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1076595-animalism-getting-creative","id":1076595,"title":"Animalism, Getting Creative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-11T11:20:14-07:00","id":1076595,"title":"Animalism, Getting Creative","content":"So, I thought I'd sit down for a bit and just come up with some uses for the Animalism Discipline, since it can be a real pain for people like myself who want mechanical examples to inspire their use beyond just textbook scenarios.<br /> <br /> So in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Guarding haven or other place in a scattered radius.<br /> Tracking targets, or monitoring area from above when near owner.<br /> Destroying soft targets (ie devour a corpse within a couple minutes, destroy the wires of many devices, eating something for retrieval later)<br /> K-9 Fighting Style bonuses (maybe? with a familiar)<br /> Tracking, Combat, Perception, and possibly some Social (ie Intimidate or Animal Ken) teamwork actions, made slightly more viable if Gangrel with Pack Alpha.<br /> If you're not particularly good at Obfuscate, masking yourself as an animal (with Protean or the Animalism/Obfuscate devotion) within a pack could be an option.<br /> <br /> If using Summon the Hunt for tracking, perhaps use your Animalism as automatic successes (provided at least 1 is rolled after penalties) on the roll or something to that effect, to signify the vast array of different animals and large amount of ground covered to simplify rolling all those dice for each animal's tracking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-11-2017, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T19:42:54-07:00","id":1076762,"title":"","content":"To me, Animalism currently and always has felt like a filler Discipline. The current 1st power is really what it's all about and could have been tucked into another Discipline like Dominate or maybe Protean(by taking on the species' form to communicate), while the other powers in every incarnation have always been odd ducks and seem to fit better as Devotions of other mind influencing Disciplines.<br /> <br /> As for uses:<br /> * - Scouts, Spies, and Couriers, though remember that they only relay information to the best of their understanding and resist commands unless ghouled or Familiar(ed?)(ized?), Destroying objects from afar, Disposing of bodies is a useful one that I hadn't considered.<br /> ** - Tough disposable shock troops, Add a bit of intelligence to an animal, Vitae delivery system for other Anm powers or ghoul feeding etc, Vitae battery(not sure if you could become addicted from your own brew)<br /> *** - Come hither<br /> **** - Crowd control, Stop a fleeing victim, General nuisance work with groups<br /> ***** - Torpor, Being a homebody,<br /> <br /> Stretching the intended limits of ***<br /> Curing or causing disease by luring microbes, viruses, spirochetes etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-11-2017, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:04:37-07:00","id":1076974,"title":"","content":"Current group is on a rather extended disease oriented arc, never though to use plague bearers to actually.. spread a plague xD<br /> With the Beasts of Blood devotion, I actually made a devotion that lets you treat your dots in Animalism as herd dots (lose 1 dot/month of the herd granted though)<br /> <br /> For couriers you could just as easily tie a coded message to them or ask them to scratch out a message on the ground in imitation of one provided - even if they don't understand what the writing means.<br /> <br /> I kind of like the Frenzy ability at 4, and it lets you give a command. Turning the street into an army of your will suddenly is bound to slow somebody down or make them think twice.<br /> I'm not sure how to rule it, but Summon the Hunt can be immensely useful during a fight, if you get them to disperse it just looks like an animal attack if it's just you and the other guy.<br /> <br /> Familiars imo make better spies only because you don't have to make them return to you to report everything constantly. Put a toothpick through a sparrow's heart and send it under the Touch of Shadow into a courthouse / wherever the info is. They can report to you in realtime through your mental connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:12:05-07:00","id":1077207,"title":"","content":"I think Animalism is the most understimated discipline ever. I think it is really powerful. <br /> <br /> 1) command to all the animals you can see to attack or distract someone. <br /> 2) great spies. <br /> 3) summon ALL the animals in a long range. It can inflict swarm condition plus dogs plus everything fits with the environment. <br /> 4) create a riot against your enemies and turn your enemies against each other. Sooo cool. <br /> 5) so thematic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:20:58-07:00","id":1077212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1076595-animalism-getting-creative?p=1077207#post1077207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Animalism is the most understimated discipline ever. I think it is really powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree, I have overlooked it in every game except my most recent one, it's actually lethal in a political game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:53:24-07:00","id":1077365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1076595-animalism-getting-creative?p=1077207#post1077207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Animalism is the most understimated discipline ever. I think it is really powerful.<br /> <br /> 1) command to all the animals you can see to attack or distract someone.<br /> 2) great spies.<br /> 3) summon ALL the animals in a long range. It can inflict swarm condition plus dogs plus everything fits with the environment.<br /> 4) create a riot against your enemies and turn your enemies against each other. Sooo cool.<br /> 5) so thematic</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm Condition? Oh, Distracted (from Swarm Form merit reference) is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:19:52-07:00","id":1077529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1076595-animalism-getting-creative?p=1077365#post1077365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Swarm Condition? Oh, Distracted (from Swarm Form merit reference) is pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm condition is taken from demon the descent core book and it specifies that this is a rule that well fits with different supernatural creatures able to control animals.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe the name is not correct. I haven't the book available now sorry. Probably is not a condition but just swarm rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-13-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:52:52-07:00","id":1077537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1076595-animalism-getting-creative?p=1077529#post1077529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Swarm condition is taken from demon the descent core book and it specifies that this is a rule that well fits with different supernatural creatures able to control animals.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe the name is not correct. I haven't the book available now sorry. Probably is not a condition but just swarm rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Tilt. I like it much better than the Swarm Form rules from Requiem. There's like, three different ways of handling swarms in three different books so far, and they're all largely similar with subtly different details. The Swarm Tilt is in my opinion the cleanest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:32:18-07:00","id":1077786,"title":"","content":"Swarm Tilt in the Sidebar p179. Bashing per turn that ignores any armour that doesn't cover the whole body, and half otherwise. Typically references only size 1 or smaller stuff, but still. When you summon say.. 7 city blocks' worth of animals that's probably a large af. swarm. I was debating using something akin to the Horde rules since Summon the Hunt brings out so much more than just bugs and birds if you want it to granted I suppose that'd just be represented as the damage being lethal instead of bashing.<br /> <br /> Demon's Primum is akin to our Blood Potency? if so a single target takes 4 bashing/lethal per turn if we use those rules. Damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-13-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}